{"type":"message","id":"79fe48d7","parentId":"dc4f34dc","timestamp":"2026-03-04T08:18:24.192Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll write the development report and save it to the shared reports directory.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-9e0b455291bb45bf9a9e02a36506c4a9","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Development Report\n\n**Date:** 2026-03-04\n**Task:** ParMETIS Algorithm Optimization - P0 Fixes\n**Agent:** code-agent\n\n## Workspace\n`/home/one/projects/cgnsMeshCutter`\n\n## Files Changed\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `src/metisCutter.cpp` | P0-1 distribute() fix, P0-2 collect_interface() refactor, P1-3 hash-based outerFace_ |\n| `src/metisCutter.h` | Added hashFace() function, updated outerFace_ data structure |\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### P0-1: Fixed `distribute()` Load Balancing\n**Problem:** Original implementation used ceiling division `(len + n - 1) / n`, causing last process to get significantly fewer elements (potentially 0 or negative).\n\n**Solution:** Implemented floor division + remainder distribution:\n```cpp\nauto base = len / n;        // Base allocation\nauto remainder = len % n;   // Remainder to distribute\nnCellThisRank = (currentRank < remainder) ? base + 1 : base;\n```\n- First `remainder` processes get `base + 1` elements\n- Remaining processes get `base` elements\n- Maximum imbalance: 1 element (optimal)\n\n### P0-2: Refactored Interface Communication\n**Problem:** Original `collect_interface()` used `MPI_Alltoallv` with O(SIZE²) communication overhead, sending complete interface data to all processes.\n\n**Solution:** Sparse point-to-point communication:\n1. **Target Rank Identification:** Each process identifies which ranks it needs to communicate with\n2. **Exchange Target Lists:** Small O(SIZE) Allgather for target rank metadata\n3. **Point-to-Point Communication:** Use `MPI_Isend/MPI_Irecv` only with processes that have shared interfaces\n4. **Binary Serialization:** Compact binary format instead of string-based serialization\n\n### P1-3: Optimized Interface Data Structure\n**Problem:** `outerFace_` used `map<string, vector<cgsize_t>>` with string keys - inefficient memory and comparison.\n\n**Solution:** Hash-based key:\n```cpp\ninline size_t hashFace(const vector<cgsize_t>& face) {\n    size_t h = 0;\n    for (auto id : face)\n        h ^= std::hash<cgsize_t>{}(id) + 0x9e3779b9 + (h << 6) + (h >> 2);\n    return h;\n}\n```\n- Changed to `unordered_map<int, map<size_t, vector<cgsize_t>>>`\n- Faster comparison (size_t vs string)\n- Reduced memory footprint\n\n## Code Notes\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n1. **P0-1:** Used local `MPI_Comm_rank` in static function since `RANK` is class member\n2. **P0-2:** Serialization includes both face hash AND face nodes for proper interface reconstruction\n3. **P1-3:** Hash function uses XOR-shift pattern for good distribution\n\n### Usage Examples\n```cpp\n// Hash-based face lookup\nauto faceHash = hashFace(face);\nif (curOuterFace.find(faceHash) != curOuterFace.end()) {\n    // Found matching interface\n}\n```\n\n## Known Limitations\n- Binary serialization assumes consistent `size_t` and `cgsize_t` sizes across all processes\n- Hash collision theoretically possible but extremely unlikely with 64-bit hash\n- Initial receive buffer size (1MB) may need adjustment for very large meshes\n\n## Performance Improvements\n| Optimization | Before | After |\n|--------------|--------|-------|\n| Load Balance | Uneven (last process starved) | Optimal (max 1 element difference) |\n| Communication | O(SIZE²) all-to-all | O(neighbors) sparse |\n| Key Lookup | String comparison | Hash comparison |\n\n## Next Steps for Team\n- **test-agent:** Verify correctness with multi-process mesh cutting tests\n- **test-agent:** Benchmark performance improvement with large meshes\n- **review-agent:** Review hash collision handling approach\n- **docs-agent:** Update README with performance characteristics\n\n## Status\n✅ Ready for testing - Code compiles successfully","file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw-reports/code-agent/2026-03-04-parmetis-optimization-p0.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":119,"output":958,"cacheRead":39487,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40564,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772612255429}}
